      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017. Publicado por Elsevier España, S.L.U.",
        "AbstractText": "HepatitisC virus infection is a significant public health problem. The introduction of direct-acting antiviral agents, whose efficacy is greater than 90% in all patient groups (including those with cirrhosis), has represented a highly relevant change compared with classical interferon-based therapies. Tolerance for these antiviral agents is significantly better, and the treatment duration is shorter. This review updates the treatment of hepatitisC virus infection with the new direct-acting antiviral agents."
      },
